#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/closure.md:2
msgctxt "s-21a074c8c5b3-0000"
msgid "Closures and lexical environments"
msgstr "Clausuras y entornos léxicos"

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/closure.md:6
msgctxt "s-71413dca3024-0001"
msgid ""
"A **closure** is a function together with the variables it was made next to."
" Those variables are its **lexical environment**: the names that were in "
"scope where the function was written. The function keeps them alive after "
"the code that made them has finished. That is why a function can remember a "
"count, a total or a seed between calls, and why nothing else can reach them."
msgstr ""
"Una **clausura** (*closure*) es una función junto con las variables que "
"tenía a su alrededor al crearse. Esas variables son su **entorno léxico**: "
"los nombres que estaban en el ámbito donde se escribió la función. La "
"función las mantiene vivas después de que termina el código que las creó. "
"Por eso una función puede recordar un conteo, un total o una semilla entre "
"llamadas y nada más puede acceder a esos datos."

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/closure.md:15
msgctxt "s-4e8dea100d8a-0002"
msgid "Two closures may share code without sharing captured state"
msgstr ""
"Dos clausuras pueden compartir código sin compartir el estado capturado"

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/closure.md:16
msgctxt "s-a2d664a412f4-0003"
msgid ""
"The function code is shared. Calling the counter factory the first time "
"makes closure A, which points to its own private environment holding n A. "
"Calling A once sets n A to 1, and calling it again sets n A to 2. Calling "
"the factory a second time makes closure B, which points to its own separate "
"environment holding n B. Calling B once sets n B to 1, and n A is not "
"changed. The factory call can return, and each environment lives while its "
"closure can be reached."
msgstr ""
"Las funciones comparten el código. La primera llamada a la fábrica de "
"contadores crea la clausura A, que apunta a su entorno privado con n A. La "
"primera llamada a A pone n A en 1 y la siguiente lo pone en 2. La segunda "
"llamada a la fábrica crea la clausura B, que apunta a su propio entorno con "
"n B. Al llamar a B una vez, n B queda en 1 y n A no cambia. La llamada a la "
"fábrica puede retornar. Cada entorno sigue vivo mientras se pueda acceder a "
"su clausura."

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/closure.md:17
msgctxt "s-ea9387face0c-0004"
msgid "shared function code: add 1 to n, return n"
msgstr "Código compartido de la función: suma 1 a n y devuelve n"

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/closure.md:20
msgctxt "s-1806cea0b15c-0005"
msgid "closure B (from factory call 2)"
msgstr "clausura B (llamada 2 a la fábrica)"

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/closure.md:20
msgctxt "s-b496771b9976-0006"
msgid "environment B: n = 0"
msgstr "entorno B: n = 0"

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/closure.md:20
msgctxt "s-4d56403cbc7e-0007"
msgid "B()"
msgstr "B()"

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/closure.md:20
msgctxt "s-f96630922dfc-0008"
msgid "n = 1"
msgstr "n = 1"

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/closure.md:21
msgctxt "s-49b6eba5a6f6-0009"
msgid "closure A (from factory call 1)"
msgstr "clausura A (llamada 1 a la fábrica)"

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/closure.md:21
msgctxt "s-d40ba82a1d0e-0010"
msgid "environment A: n = 0"
msgstr "entorno A: n = 0"

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/closure.md:21
msgctxt "s-b9ee44d39137-0011"
msgid "A()"
msgstr "A()"

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/closure.md:21
msgctxt "s-f96630922dfc-0012"
msgid "n = 1"
msgstr "n = 1"

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/closure.md:21
msgctxt "s-b9ee44d39137-0013"
msgid "A()"
msgstr "A()"

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/closure.md:21
msgctxt "s-0d3332659264-0014"
msgid "n = 2"
msgstr "n = 2"

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/closure.md:24
msgctxt "s-dcb5e41df970-0015"
msgid ""
"Each box under a closure is that closure's *own* environment. The number is "
"not copied into the code when the closure is made. The factory's call frame "
"can return, and the captured variable lives on while the closure can be "
"reached. These are two different factory calls. Two functions made in *one* "
"factory call over the same variable would share it, as described below."
msgstr ""
"Cada cuadro debajo de una clausura es su *propio* entorno. Al crear la "
"clausura, el número no se copia al código. El marco de la llamada a la "
"fábrica puede retirarse y la variable capturada sigue viva mientras se pueda"
" acceder a la clausura. Son dos llamadas distintas a la fábrica. Dos "
"funciones creadas en *una sola* llamada a la fábrica que capturaran la misma"
" variable la compartirían, como se explica abajo."

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/closure.md:26
msgctxt "s-f60f0e6f55be-0016"
msgid "Be exact about three things:"
msgstr "Sé preciso en tres puntos:"

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/closure.md:28
msgctxt "s-4083755dfb71-0017"
msgid ""
"**A closure captures variables, not values.** Two closures over the same "
"variable share it, and a change made by one is seen by the other. Each call "
"to a factory such as ⟦CODE_0001⟧ makes a *new* variable, so two counters "
"never share state. C# lambdas behave the same way."
msgstr ""
"**Una clausura captura variables, no valores.** Dos clausuras que capturan "
"la misma variable la comparten. Si una la cambia, la otra ve el cambio. Cada"
" llamada a una fábrica como ⟦CODE_0001⟧ crea una variable *nueva*, así que "
"dos contadores nunca comparten estado. Las lambdas de C# se comportan igual."

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/closure.md:29
msgctxt "s-ca98703be657-0018"
msgid ""
"**Lambda syntax is not a closure.** ⟦CODE_0001⟧ uses no outside variable, so"
" there is nothing interesting to capture. An arrow function that updates a "
"variable that outlives the call is a closure that matters."
msgstr ""
"**La sintaxis lambda no es una clausura.** ⟦CODE_0001⟧ no usa ninguna "
"variable externa, así que no hay nada interesante que capturar. Una función "
"flecha que actualiza una variable que sobrevive a la llamada sí es una "
"clausura que importa."

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/closure.md:30
msgctxt "s-72aa058f375d-0019"
msgid ""
"**A closure is not a continuation.** You can call it again and it does the "
"*next* step. You cannot hand it \"the rest of the computation\", resume it "
"in the middle of something or go back. See ⟦MACRO_0001⟧. Nor is ⟦CODE_0002⟧ "
"a captured variable: a method that uses ⟦CODE_0003⟧ loses its ⟦CODE_0004⟧ "
"when you detach it from its object, and a closure keeps its variable."
msgstr ""
"**Una clausura no es una continuación.** Puedes volver a llamarla y "
"ejecutará el paso *siguiente*. No puedes entregarle \"el resto del "
"cálculo\", reanudarla a mitad de algo ni volver atrás. Consulta "
"⟦MACRO_0001⟧. ⟦CODE_0002⟧ tampoco es una variable capturada. Un método que "
"usa ⟦CODE_0003⟧ pierde su ⟦CODE_0004⟧ cuando lo separas de su objeto, "
"mientras que una clausura conserva su variable."

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/closure.md:32
msgctxt "s-397ed03549c8-0020"
msgid ""
"The environment lives as long as the function can be reached. When nothing "
"refers to the function any more, the engine may collect it, and its "
"variables with it. ⟦MACRO_0001⟧ builds its whole algorithm from three "
"closures (a seeded number source, a card machine and an iterator around it),"
" and its check script proves each claim on this page, including the lifetime"
" one, with a ⟦CODE_0002⟧ and a forced garbage collection. ⟦MACRO_0003⟧ uses "
"a closure over the seed for its random numbers. ⟦MACRO_0004⟧ and "
"⟦MACRO_0005⟧ use closures (and a C# lambda) to move work into places that "
"expect a value."
msgstr ""
"El entorno vive mientras se pueda acceder a la función. Cuando nada apunta a"
" la función, el motor puede recuperar su memoria y la de sus variables. "
"⟦MACRO_0001⟧ arma todo su algoritmo con tres clausuras: una fuente de "
"números con semilla, una máquina de tarjetas y un iterador que la envuelve. "
"Su script de comprobación demuestra cada afirmación de esta página, incluida"
" la del tiempo de vida, con un ⟦CODE_0002⟧ y una recolección de basura "
"forzada. ⟦MACRO_0003⟧ usa una clausura que captura la semilla de sus números"
" aleatorios. ⟦MACRO_0004⟧ y ⟦MACRO_0005⟧ usan clausuras (y una lambda de C#)"
" para llevar trabajo a lugares que esperan un valor."

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/closure.md:34
msgctxt "s-9673b2209dbb-0021"
msgid ""
"**Use it when:** you need private state without a class, a function that is "
"configured once and called many times or a callback that must remember "
"something."
msgstr ""
"**Úsala cuando:** necesites estado privado sin una clase, una función que "
"configuras una vez y llamas muchas veces o una función de devolución de "
"llamada (*callback*) que deba recordar algo."

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/closure.md:35
msgctxt "s-48200c7f9053-0022"
msgid ""
"**Avoid it when:** the hidden state makes the program hard to test or to "
"read. Captured variables do not show up in a debugger the way fields do, and"
" a long chain of closures is hard to follow."
msgstr ""
"**Evítala cuando:** el estado oculto haga difícil probar o leer el programa."
" Las variables capturadas no aparecen en el depurador como los campos. Una "
"cadena larga de clausuras es difícil de seguir."

